description: Pragmatic Matt Pocock TDD for features and bug fixes
alwaysApply: true
---

# TDD (pragmatic)

- New pure/domain logic and bug fixes: one failing test → minimal code → refactor (vertical slices).
- Test behavior through public interfaces, not internals.
- Skip test-first for UI wiring, config, and copy-only changes.
- Do not write large batches of tests before any implementation.
- Prefer extending `backend/tests/` and frontend `*.test.ts` under Vitest.
- Manual Live/Gemini flows stay in `backend/scripts/` — not a substitute for unit tests.
